The SDFGI investigation's animations
====================================

The viewer's Play animation of each demonstration (its file's `animation`): the values at the demonstration's
time `t`, in seconds, each a sine wave about its centre (`wave center amplitude period t`).

$[Import* std]$[Import* render_lab_runtime]$[Import* godot_sdfgi_values]

SDFGI's simulated camera walk, `cameraX`: the values package names `setCameraX` after the orbit camera's
`camera.x`, so this writes the investigation's own value by its key.
$[# {_setWalk x} {: {. key "cameraX" value {toData {: x Float}}} Write}]

SDFGI's light faded in and out.
$[# playMix {: {^ {t} {' {setSdfgiMix {wave 0.5 0.5 10.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The camera walks along x, so cascade 0 jumps one probe each 1.6 m.
$[# playWalk {: {^ {t} {' {_setWalk {wave 0.0 4.0 20.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The cut through the voxels rises and falls.
$[# playVoxels {: {^ {t} {' {setCutHeight {wave 2.0 2.0 12.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The distance field's slice rises and falls.
$[# playField {: {^ {t} {' {setSliceHeight {wave 1.2 1.0 14.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The occlusion's shells, one after another.
$[# playOcclusion {: {^ {t} {' {setOcclusionShell {wave 11.0 11.0 12.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The light moves across the room.
$[# playLight {: {^ {t} {' {setLightX {wave 0.0 2.6 14.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The probes' rays, frame after frame.
$[# playProbes {: {^ {t} {' {setRayFrames {wave 15.0 15.0 16.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The maps converge, frame after frame.
$[# playMaps {: {^ {t} {' {setFrames {wave 30.0 30.0 16.0 t}}}} Animation}]

The worked pixel moves along the floor.
$[# playPixel {: {^ {t} {' {setPixelZ {wave 0.0 2.6 16.0 t}}}} Animation}]
